### ==============================================================================
### DecisionHub Backend API Test Suite
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 1. HEALTH CHECKS & SYSTEM STATUS
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Root Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 1.2 Health Check (v1 API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health HTTP/1.1

### 1.3 Health Check (Legacy Path)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health HTTP/1.1



### ==============================================================================
### 2. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Register New User - Success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.2 Register User - Duplicate Email (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Duplicate",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.3 Register User - Validation Error (Invalid Email & Short Password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 2.4 Login User - Success (Captures JWT token for subsequent requests)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store the JWT token from login response
@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhbGljZUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc5NDgyNjkyMywiZXhwIjoxNzk0OTEzMzIzfQ.6VQLZvsnOqURT7TKMRORwkprUS6FIqNO94tUmiuR5u4

### 2.5 Login User - Incorrect Password (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 2.6 Login User - Unknown Email (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent.user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ==============================================================================
### 3. PROTECTED ENDPOINTS & AUTHORIZATION CHECKS
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Protected Endpoint Without Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Protected Endpoint With Invalid Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid-or-tampered-token-12345

### 3.3 Protected Endpoint With Valid Bearer Token (Passes Security Filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}



### ==============================================================================
### 4. DECISION BOARD MANAGEMENT (MILESTONE 2 - PHASE 1)
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Create Decision - Success (PUBLIC with initial options)
# @name createDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Select Core Backend Architecture",
  "description": "Choose between Monolith vs Microservices for high scale deployment.",
  "category": "Technology",
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "pollType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
  "options": [
    {
      "title": "Modular Monolith",
      "description": "High cohesion, single deployment unit, easy refactoring",
      "displayOrder": 0
    },
    {
      "title": "Microservices",
      "description": "Independently deployable bounded contexts with event bus",
      "displayOrder": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Store the created decision ID
@decisionId = 229

### 4.2 Create Decision - Validation Failure (Blank fields, Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": ""
}

### 4.3 Create Decision - Unauthenticated (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Decision",
  "description": "Should be rejected without valid token",
  "category": "Security"
}

### 4.4 Retrieve Public Decisions (Paginated, Public Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/public?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=desc HTTP/1.1

### 4.5 Retrieve Decisions (Authenticated Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions?page=0&size=10 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.6 Retrieve Decisions Created by Authenticated User
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/my?page=0&size=10 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.7 Retrieve Decision by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.8 Retrieve Decision by Missing ID (Expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/999999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.9 Update Decision (Creator or Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Select Core Backend Architecture (Updated)",
  "description": "Updated context with deployment metrics and cost analysis.",
  "category": "Technology",
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 4.10 Delete Decision (Creator or Admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### 5. OPTION MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Add Multiple Options to Decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "options": [
    {
      "title": "Serverless Functions",
      "description": "Event-driven compute scaled to zero when idle",
      "displayOrder": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Edge Compute",
      "description": "Distributed edge nodes for ultra-low latency",
      "displayOrder": 3
    }
  ]
}

### 5.2 Retrieve All Options for Decision
# @name getOptions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Store Option ID (Use the ID of an option returned in Step 5.2 or Step 4.1 above)
@optionId = 174

### 5.3 Update Option within Decision
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Modular Monolith (Optimized)",
  "description": "Single repository with Spring Modulith boundaries",
  "displayOrder": 0
}

### 5.4 Update Option - Cross-Decision Mismatch (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/99999 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Option Not Belonging to Decision",
  "description": "Should fail with 400 Bad Request"
}

### 5.5 Delete Option within Decision
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### 6. OPTION COMPARISON & EVALUATION MATRIX (MILESTONE 2 - PHASE 2)
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 Initialize Default Comparison Criteria (COST, BENEFITS, RISK, TIME, CONVENIENCE)
# @name createDefaultCriteria
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/criteria/default HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.2 Create Custom Comparison Criterion (e.g. Scalability)
# @name createCustomCriterion
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/criteria HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "SCALABILITY",
  "description": "Ability to handle 10x traffic bursts with linear resource scaling",
  "weight": 20.0,
  "minScore": 1.0,
  "maxScore": 10.0,
  "polarity": "HIGHER_IS_BETTER"
}

### Store Criterion ID
@criterionId = 6

### 6.3 Retrieve All Criteria for Decision
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/criteria HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.4 Update Criterion (Adjust weight and description)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/criteria/{{criterionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "SCALABILITY",
  "description": "Horizontal and vertical autoscaling under high throughput",
  "weight": 25.0,
  "minScore": 1.0,
  "maxScore": 10.0,
  "polarity": "HIGHER_IS_BETTER"
}

### 6.5 Upsert Qualitative Comparison Data for Option
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/comparison HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "featureValues": "Single JAR deployment, JVM memory tuning, HikariCP pool",
  "costDetails": "Low operational cost: runs on single container instance",
  "benefitDetails": "Extremely fast development cycles, zero distributed transaction overhead",
  "riskDetails": "Single point of failure; vertical scaling ceiling",
  "timeDetails": "2 weeks initial MVP delivery",
  "convenienceDetails": "Simple debugging, single Git repository, seamless IDE navigation"
}

### 6.6 Retrieve Qualitative Comparison Data for Option
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/comparison HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.7 Add Advantage (Pro) to Option
# @name addProOption
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/pros-cons HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "type": "PRO",
  "description": "Fast ACID transactions without distributed consensus protocols",
  "displayOrder": 0
}

### Store Pro ID
@proId = {{addProOption.response.body.data.id}}

### 6.8 Add Disadvantage (Con) to Option
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/pros-cons HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "type": "CON",
  "description": "Deployment coupling: all modules must restart simultaneously on update",
  "displayOrder": 1
}

### 6.9 Retrieve All Pros and Cons for Option
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/pros-cons HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.10 Update Pro/Con Entry
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/pros-cons/{{proId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "type": "PRO",
  "description": "Strict ACID guarantees with ultra-low latency local DB transactions",
  "displayOrder": 0
}

### 6.11 Set Criteria Scores for Option (Modular Monolith)
### Note: Replace criterionId values with the IDs returned from Step 6.1 or 6.3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/scores HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "scores": [
    {
      "criterionId": 1,
      "rawScore": 2.0,
      "notes": "Very cost effective on standard VM"
    },
    {
      "criterionId": 2,
      "rawScore": 8.0,
      "notes": "Excellent feature velocity"
    },
    {
      "criterionId": 3,
      "rawScore": 3.0,
      "notes": "Low operational risk"
    },
    {
      "criterionId": 4,
      "rawScore": 2.0,
      "notes": "Quick implementation timeframe"
    },
    {
      "criterionId": 5,
      "rawScore": 9.0,
      "notes": "Highly convenient local development"
    }
  ]
}

### 6.12 Retrieve Option Numerical Scores
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/scores HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.13 Retrieve Complete Evaluation & Comparison Matrix
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/comparison-matrix HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.14 Retrieve Deterministic Ranked Options
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/rankings HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.15 Delete Criterion
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/criteria/{{criterionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6.16 Delete Pro/Con Entry
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/{{optionId}}/pros-cons/{{proId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
